{
  "version": "1.9.7",
  "changelog": "Delete now SHOWS you the road before anything is removed. Click a road to select it, press the Delete button, and the map frames the whole road \u2014 zooming in or out like a photograph with a little of the surrounding streets \u2014 and lights it up in bright pink, with the road's name and the Delete/Cancel choice in a slim bar at the top of the map. Cancel puts the view back exactly where it was. The old Pan and Select modes are gone: dragging the map always moves it, clicking a road always selects it, and Delete is one button that works on whatever is selected (with nothing selected it simply says 'Nothing is selected'). Picking a road can no longer freeze the editor \u2014 a click only registers the pick, the picture is prepared in the background \u2014 and a progress bar in the bottom-right corner now shows whenever the editor is downloading, pushing, or preparing something heavy, so a busy app never looks frozen.",
